{"_v":1,"id":"one-man-two-guvnors-2012","cat":"broadway","cs":86.53,"rc":16,"bd":{"positive":15,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Adam Feldman","o":"Time Out New York","s":97,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/one-man-two-guvnors","d":"2012-04-18","q":"How starved we were for comedy."},{"cn":"David Rooney","o":"The Hollywood Reporter","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/one-man-two-guvnors-theater-review-313775","d":"2012-04-18","q":"If you’re not having a good time at this show, you may be on the wrong medication."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2012/04/19/theater/reviews/james-corden-in-one-man-two-guvnors-at-the-music-box.html","d":"2012-04-18","q":"Letting loose and neutralizing all sorts of demons, it’s ideal escapism for anxious times."},{"cn":"Jesse Green","o":"Vulture","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.vulture.com/2012/04/stage-dive-theater-review-one-man-two-guvnors.html","d":"2012-04-18","q":"Artisanal rib-tickling, prepared fresh, before your eyes, and a bit different every night."},{"cn":"Mark Kennedy","o":"Associated Press","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/theater_dance/review-gleeful-comedy-in-joyously-slapstick-british-export-one-man-two-guvnors/2012/04/18/gIQAfv1jRT_story.html","d":"2012-04-18"},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"The Guardian","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2012/apr/19/one-man-two-guvnors-broadway-opening","d":"2012-04-19","q":"I dare you to see it and not laugh out loud, a lot."},{"cn":"Matt Windman","o":"Newsday","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newsday.com/news/new-york/theater-review-one-man-two-guvnors-3-5-stars-v30010","d":"2012-04-18","q":"There's the squeaky dry, silly-smart kind we know from Monty Python, Michael Frayn and Tom Stoppard. I love that kind. Then there is the slapstick, pants-dropping, music-hall, silly-dumb sort that traces its stock-character, low-comedy pedigree back ..."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.newsday.com/entertainment/theater/one-man-two-guvnors-is-pure-slapstick-1.3667079","d":"2012-04-18","q":"Virtuosic fun for low-comedy addicts only"},{"cn":"Lisa Schwarzbaum","o":"Entertainment Weekly","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.ew.com/ew/article/0,,20364394_20588357,00.html","d":"2012-04-18","q":"You'll know smart hilarity when you're guffawing at it."},{"cn":"Howard Shapiro","o":"The Philadelphia Inquirer","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://articles.philly.com/2012-04-18/news/31361936_1_new-broadway-show-actors-cast","d":"2012-04-18","q":"Whatever it is, I dare you to see it and not laugh out loud, a lot."},{"cn":"David Sheward","o":"Backstage","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.backstage.com/bso/reviews-ny-theatre-broadway/ny-review-one-man-two-guvnors-1006806572.story","q":"The Music Box management should be required to install restraints for the seats, as you're likely to be falling out of yours from laughing so hard."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/OneManTwoGuvnors.html","d":"2012-05-06","q":"James Corden is a marvel of physical comedy and vocal dexterity, turning what could be a one-note farce into something approaching theatrical magic."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.nydailynews.com/2012/04/18/review-one-man-two-guvnors-and-countless-laughs-on-broadway/","d":"2012-04-19","q":"Hail to the clown prince of this royal scream."},{"cn":"Michael Musto","o":"Village Voice","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://blogs.villagevoice.com/dailymusto/2012/04/one_man_two_guv.php","q":"Guvnors often has you hoarse from laughing, and allows you the rare chance to brag about seeing something extremely tony that also happens to be incredibly Benny."},{"cn":"Samuel L. Leiter","o":"Stage and Cinema","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://stageandcinema.com/2012/04/19/one-man-two-guvnors-broadway/","d":"2012-04-30","q":"One Man, Two Guvnors is smart, it’s charming, and most importantly, it’s very funny!"},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New Jersey Newsroom","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.newjerseynewsroom.com/new-york-theater/review-one-man-two-guvnors-delivers-laughter","d":"2012-04-18","q":"“One Man, Two Guvnors” proves to be an extremely funny entertainment likely to banish (temporarily) whatever problems irk you."}],"au":{"score":85,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":85,"c":33,"sr":4.3}}},"tn":[{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Actor in a Play","n":"James Corden","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"Grant Olding"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Featured Actor in a Play","n":"Tom Edden"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Direction of a Play","n":"Nicholas Hytner"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Scenic Design of a Play","n":"Mark Thompson"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Costume Design of a Play","n":"Mark Thompson"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Sound Design of a Play","n":"Paul Arditti"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":null}],"cn":{"t":"Critics unanimously praise this uproarious farce as the season's funniest show, with James Corden delivering a virtuosic comic performance and Nicholas Hytner's staging balancing meticulous planning with anarchic spontaneity.","rc":21},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":13071416,"p":172,"a":140382}},"ta":"239 W 45th St, New York, NY 10036","vs":{"sl":4,"so":3,"co":3,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2012-04-06","ca":[{"n":"James Corden","r":"Francis Henshall"},{"n":"Oliver Chris","r":"Stanley Stubbers"},{"n":"Jemima Rooper","r":"Rachel Crabbe"},{"n":"Tom Edden","r":"Alfie"},{"n":"Martyn Ellis","r":"Harry Dangle"},{"n":"Eli James","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Trevor Laird","r":"Lloyd Boateng"},{"n":"Claire Lams","r":"Pauline Clench"},{"n":"Ben Livingston","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Sarah Manton","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Stephen Pilkington","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Fred Ridgeway","r":"Charlie \"the Duck\" Clench"},{"n":"Daniel Rigby","r":"Alan Dangle"},{"n":"David Ryan Smith","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Natalie Smith","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Suzie Toase","r":"Dolly"}]}